{
 "_readme": "Centennial Campus podium (CPD) floor plans: HKU Examinations Office's classroom plans (Feb 2017), scanned pages, one per floor. M registers each page, rendered at dpi, to the model frame: x = a*u - b*v + tx, z = b*u + a*v + tz (u, v = rendered pixels). 2/F was fitted to the surveyed sections of the podium and towers (B31881..., B31817..., B31887..., B31911...); the other pages to 2/F through the column grid, cores and atria they share (LG/F through G/F). y = floor level in mPD: LG/F is +84.50 as marked on the plan, 4/F is the podium roof (107 m, where the towers stand) and the floors between are spread evenly (estimated). clip: the podium and towers' footprint from the model. holes: the atria (1/F to 3/F; on G/F their floors are gardens), from the model's sections, the east one (open to the courtyard side, so not a closed loop in the model) as the middle one moved to where the plans draw it. rooms: classrooms traced by hand on the rendered page (pixels) where the scan doesn't close them off. walls: wall polylines traced by hand on each page (rendered pixels) and snapped to the ink; notes: [name, u, v] small-print room names read off the page.",
